A||||9||David DeVoe||2.5 erratic idle and horrendous flat spot||||5||
Z||000000||David DeVoe||12-16-2001||06:48 PM||||This is driving me nuts. The base idle is high maybe 1500 and then the idle hunts up and down. Also have a tremendous dead spot on acceleration. The computer set codes 33 & 34 both of which relate to the MAP sensor. I changed it but no joy. The engine is in a 91 <BR>S10 (I know) but I thought one of the Duke guys might be able to help. I hate to just change gizmos (they're expensive)The damn thing is almost undrivable. Anyone???<BR>Dave<BR>86 SE||||reg||5
Z||000001||johnt671||12-16-2001||07:10 PM||||Try the no cost stuff first.  Look for vacuum leaks in any of the vacuum line, and remove the IAC valve from the throttle body and clean both it and the area it screws into.  Put it back together and go for a drive.  It takes a little trip to reset the IAC and you must go over 35 mph to set it.  Check the bolts holding down the throttle body and be sure they are tight.  Pull a plug and see if it is black or wet from running rich.  If so you may want to check fuel pressure and the coolant temp sensor for the ECM.  If this fails you will run rich.  Try the no cost stuff first and read the plugs and see what happens.||||reg||1
Z||000002||David DeVoe||12-16-2001||07:15 PM||||good stuff JohnT. The plugs are new, nice and tan, engine starts right up, the problem mostly occurrs after warmup. I'll check the vacuum lines again. Id love to find one of those suckers off or broken.<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||12-16-2001||07:44 PM||||I had a similar problem with my 84, but not as bad.  Checked everything and replace the IAC and still had a bit of hunting.  The last thing I could think of was to replace the gasket under the throttle body.  When I took it off I found the EGR passages under it were all carbon closed.  Cleaned them up and put the new gasket on and the idle got much better.  Maybe worth the 8 bucks I spent.  How old is your oxygen sensor?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTDude||12-16-2001||08:01 PM||||Every time i've seen a code 33 and 34 together it's been either the map sensor or ecm.  Could be other causes....but this is my personal experience.  Good luck.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||David DeVoe||12-16-2001||11:56 PM||||Good question. The o2 sensor is original, got about 62k on it. In fact everything on the engine except the plugs, air cleaner and belt is original. I'll look into the throttle body thing if I can't find anything else.<BR>Thanks guys<BR>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000006||watts||12-17-2001||01:20 AM||||Check your EGR valve as well - if it gets clogged open, it acts like a big ass vaccum leak that you can just never track down.<P>Been tricked by it before...<P>So pull it out, clean the pintle and seat with carb cleaner (same thing on the IAC).  Pour some solvent in it (the EGR valve) and see if it leaks much.  If it'll more or less hold fluid, it'll more or less not leak air.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||dcaprio||12-17-2001||07:59 AM||||With the car running take off the oil fill cap and make sure you don't have a lot of blow-by ( a lot of smoke coming out ). If you do then it's an internal problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||12-17-2001||08:25 PM||||There is a very critical differance between the car and truck versions that I've seen of the 2.5l DIS motor.....<P>The truck uses an EGR solinoid like the Fiero V6 does.<P>First think is start with making sure all the vac lines are good and so on. <P>Make sure the EGR solinoid isn't leaking vacuum to the EGR. EGR should not open at idle.<P>Check PCV line carfully. clamp all joints. (Gently... elbows are soft...)<P>beyond that, you'll need at least the haynes book for the truck.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000009||David DeVoe||12-18-2001||02:01 AM||||Thanks Ogre,<BR>I have the haynes manual and the trouble shooting section is imho a joke but it at least was a start. I'll look very closely at the egr valve, that seems to come up a lot on the forum.||||reg||1
